From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 14:16:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: drop queue->mutex before the eventfd write in
 tapdisk_vbd_kick

The producer wake (write to queue->efd) was done while still holding
queue->mutex, serialising every completion's kick against the producer
thread, which also takes queue->mutex. The eventfd write needs no lock
(it is atomic), so unlock right after draining completed_requests and do
the write outside the critical section. Also drops the now-redundant
unlock in the efd < 0 early return.
---
 drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c b/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
index d7ddfe2e..b004299a 100644
--- a/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
+++ b/drivers/tapdisk-vbd.c
@@ -2149,19 +2149,18 @@ tapdisk_vbd_kick(td_vbd_queue_t *queue, bool scheduler_kick)
 		prev->cb(prev, prev->error, prev->token, 1);
 		queue->returned++;
 	}
+	pthread_mutex_unlock(&queue->mutex);
 
 	if (scheduler_kick && td_flag_test(vbd->driver_flags, TD_DRIVER_THREADED)) {
 		static uint64_t token = 1;
 
 		if (queue->efd < 0) {
-		    pthread_mutex_unlock(&queue->mutex);
 		    return;
 		}
 
 		s = write(queue->efd, &token, sizeof(uint64_t));
 		ASSERT(s == sizeof(uint64_t));
 	}
-	pthread_mutex_unlock(&queue->mutex);
 }
 
 int
